  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-263",
  "title": "Akshay Kothari Interview",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Akshay Kothari Interview"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wY_pslf3n1o](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wY_pslf3n1o)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Founder Mode & Leadership:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- \"Founder Mode\" (a high-conviction, founder-driven approach) is highly effective if the founder has a strong track record of being \"right a lot.\" If not, it can be detrimental."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Akshay's role as COO was to scale the business and company, allowing his co-founders (Ivan and Simon) to focus intensely on the product."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Operational Efficiency & Cash Management:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Notion has \"more cash in its bank today than the history of its raise,\" meaning they've \"produced cash\" rather than just spent venture capital. This highlights exceptional capital efficiency."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Fundraising can be strategic, not just out of necessity. Notion raised $50M at a $2B valuation during early COVID, not primarily for cash needs, but as a signal of stability to attract top talent flocking to safety."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Learning Across Disciplines & Systems Thinking:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Akshay, despite a product background, took on diverse roles (CMO, CFO, CHRO, etc.) by applying first-principles thinking and systems design learned from product development."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- *Example: Customer Support.* Instead of just hiring more people as support tickets grew, they built a system to categorize ~200 request types, tag them, and feed this data directly to engineers for product improvement, allowing for a leaner support team."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **Hiring & Team Building:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **High Standards:** Notion maintained a very high bar for hiring, with founders (Ivan or Akshay) involved in the final interview up to 500 employees. They were willing to \"endure the pain\" of waiting for truly \"great\" talent."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Lean Team:** A core philosophy was keeping the team small and nimble, believing it allows for faster, more focused execution. (e.g., under 20 PMs and 12 designers for the entire Notion product, including Calendar)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. **Sales Function Evolution (Learning from Mistakes):**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Akshay regrets not building a traditional, quota-driven sales team earlier."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- They initially tried a more consultative sales approach without quotas, believing the product-led growth would suffice."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- He learned that top salespeople are often motivated by hitting and exceeding quotas, and a more structured \"sales machine\" would have accelerated their enterprise efforts significantly."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "6. **Investor & Board Philosophy:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Investor Quality:** They value top-tier investors like Sequoia and Coatue, who demand excellence, aligning with Notion's own high standards."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Board Composition:** They were deliberate about board seats, not automatically granting them based on investment size, preferring to \"recruit\" board members who could act as one-on-one coaches for the executive team in specific functional areas (e.g., CEO coach, audit chair, GTM expert)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "7. **Strategic Patience & Long-Term Vision:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Notion is playing a long-term game, focused on building a \"generational company.\" This allows them to make decisions that might have short-term costs (like slower hiring) for long-term benefits."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Being cash-flow positive early on provided them the \"control of their destiny,\" allowing them to raise capital on their own terms and when strategically beneficial, rather than out of necessity."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "8. **Broader Concerns (TikTokification):**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Akshay expressed concern about the \"TikTokification\" of social media, where platforms are optimized for attention time via infinite streams of viral videos, potentially leading to an imbalanced \"consumption to creation ratio\" in society."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "9. **Contextual Advice:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Most startup advice is highly contextual. What works for one company or founder might be \"genius\" for them but \"rubbish\" for others. Founders need to discern what's applicable to their specific situation."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}